===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|blanket}}, {{m|enm|blonket}}, {{m|enm|blaunket}}, from {{der|en|fro-nor|-}} {{m|fro|blanket}}, {{m|fro|blancet|t=white horse", also "white woollen cloth or flannel; a type of jacket|lit=that which is white}} (whence Modern {{cog|fr|blanchet}}), diminutive of {{m|fro|blanc|t=white}}, of {{der|en|gem|-}} origin (compare {{cog|ang|blanca|t=white horse}}; see more at {{m|en|blank}}). Furthermore, likely a {{calque|en|ang|hwītel|t=cloak, mantle|nocap=1|nocat=1}}, from {{m+|ang|hwīt|t=white}} + {{m|ang|-el|pos=diminutive suffix}}. Compare also {{cog|non|hvítill|t=a white bed-cover, sheet}}.

Compare also {{m|en|blunket}}, {{m|en|plunket}}. Displaced native {{ncog|enm|whytel}}, from {{ncog|ang|hwītel}} (whence Modern {{m+|en|whittle|t=blanket, cloak, shawl}}).

