===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{senseid|en|Q5852}}A heavy, loosely woven fabric, usually large and woollen, used for [[warmth]] while [[sleeping]] or resting.
#: {{ux|en|The baby was cold, so his mother put a '''blanket''' over him.}}
#* {{RQ:Woolf Jacob's Room|1||The little boys in the front bedroom had thrown off their '''blankets''' and lay under the sheets.}}
# A [[layer]] of anything.
#: {{ux|en|The city woke under a thick '''blanket''' of fog.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=1948|month=March and April|title=Noes and News: Slab Blanketing at Clapham Junction|journal=Railway Magazine|page=131|text=In this case, the excavations were carried down to a depth of 3 ft. 9 in. below rail level, and pre-cast concrete slabs were laid between a 12 in. '''blanket''' of quarry waste and the ballast.}}
# A thick rubber mat used in the offset printing process to transfer ink from the [[plate]] to the paper being printed.
#: {{ux|en|A press operator must carefully wash the '''blanket''' whenever changing a plate.}}
# A [[streak]] or [[layer]] of [[blubber]] in [[whale]]s.

